p_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":88.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.04678,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":31.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"MillerKnoll, Inc. researches, designs, manufactures, sells, and distributes interior furnishings worldwide. It operates through North America Contract, International Contract, and Global Retail segments. The company also provides seating products, furniture systems, other freestanding furniture elements, textiles, leather, felt, home furnishings and related services; and casegoods, storage products, and acoustic products and related services, as well as residential, education, and healthcare furniture solutions. It offers its products under the MillerKnoll, Herman Miller, Knoll, Maharam, Geiger, Design Within Reach, HAY, NaughtOne, Colebrook Bosson Saunders, Holly Hunt, Muuto, FilzFelt, Edelman, Spinneybeck, and KnollTextiles brand names. The company offers its products through independent contract furniture dealers, direct contract sales, owned and independent retailers, direct-mail catalogs, and e-commerce platforms. Its products are used in institutional, health/science, industrial and educational settings, and residential and other environments. The company was formerly known as Herman Miller, Inc. and changed its name to MillerKnoll, Inc. in November 2021. MillerKnoll, Inc. was incorporated in 1905 and is headquartered in Zeeland, Michigan.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey M. Stutz | CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $971,408 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $364K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $7K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["MillerKnoll, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.4B market cap on $3.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 37%.","The business throws off $78M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 40% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 20% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (MLKN) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/16/Understanding_the_Setup:_MLKN_and_Scalable_Risk_112226114002_1795365602.html","date":"2026-11-22","timestamp":1795365602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (MLKN)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_MLKN_111226010002_1794506402.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794506402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MillerKnoll (NASDAQ:MLKN) Stock Rating Lowered by Wall Street Zen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/millerknoll-nasdaqmlkn-stock